==English==
[[File:Angola w2 locator.svg|thumb|right|Angola]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|pt|Angola|(Reino de) Angola|(kingdom of) Angola}}, from {{der|en|kmb|ngola|}}, title held by native kings at the time of the Portuguese colonization in the 15th century AD.<ref>{{R:Etymonline|entry=Angola|accessdate=30 July 2019}}</ref> Compare {{cog|ktu|ngolo||strength}}.

The Louisiana State Penitentiary is named "Angola" after the Angola slave plantation it replaced, which was named after the country, from which many enslaved people in Louisiana had been taken.

